  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts as an Aura3D orrery. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so I haven't seen it render.\n\n- **Star:** an emissive sphere at the centre with a point light inside it. A bloom effect on a near-black `#03040a` background gives it the glow.\n- **Planets:** five spheres of different sizes and colours, on radii from 2.8 to 10.4 at different speeds. Each is updated every frame with `app.onFrame`.\n- **Ring:** the fourth planet (\"saturn\") has a flattened torus ring that follows it and is tilted.\n- **Camera:** a perspective camera at [0, 15, 17] looking at the origin, meant to frame the outermost orbit. I haven't checked that framing in a render.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true one animation frame after the first frame callback.\n\nThe scene draws into the existing `#app` canvas.\n\nI assumed the torus is a ring in the local XY plane with a major radius of 0.43, going by the engine source. I rotated it to lie flat, but I haven't seen the result. If the ring looks too thick or too thin, adjust the `size` of the torus in `src/main.ts`.\n\n",
